-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles level comparison: M_Q(Hᵣ)≅ M, T_ℓ-equivariantly
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the absolute Galois group of some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline k$ has no Galois-stable submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S$, let $N\neq 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $p\nmid r-1$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$, none equal to $r$, each congruent to $1$ in $k$, and let $\alpha_i\in k$ satisfy $\alpha_i^2-\theta(T_{q_i})\alpha_i+q_i=0$ and $2\alpha_i\neq\theta(T_{q_i})$. Assume finally that the operators indexed by the auxiliary-level generators (primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq r$) commute on $H^1$ of level $Nr$ with the subgroup $\mathrm{subgroup}\,N\,r$. Put $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$ and $H_R=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times\big)$. The assertion is that for every proof `hcR` that the operators indexed by $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$) and $U_i$ ($i<t$) commute on $H^1(L,H_R,\mathcal O)$, there is an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the Taylor–Wiles-level module `ML`, the localisation of $H^1(L,H_R,\mathcal O)$ at the prime complement of the kernel `mTheta` of the map from $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}$ in those generators over $\mathcal O$ to $k$ attached to the eigensystem sending $X_{T_\ell}\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$ and $X_{U_i}\mapsto\alpha_i$, onto the corresponding auxiliary-level module [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.ML`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L46) for $\theta$ at level $Nr$, such that $e$ is equivariant for the Hecke variables away from $L$: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and every $x$, $e(X_{T_\ell}\cdot x)=X_{\ell}\cdot e(x)$, where on the right $\ell$ is viewed as an auxiliary-level generator using $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq r$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the $\mathfrak m$-localised cohomology at a Taylor–Wiles level $L=N(\prod q_i)r$ with that at the auxiliary level $Nr$ (the "$\alpha$-stabilisation" at the Taylor–Wiles primes $q_i$), here for the anemic eigensystem of an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$ with the prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials, and with the isomorphism recorded as equivariant for the Hecke variables at primes away from $L$. It feeds the construction of a monoid-algebra basis of the Taylor–Wiles-level module together with the comparison map to the auxiliary level, in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_basis_ML_monoidAlgebra_and_linearMap_ML_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_basis_ML_monoidAlgebra_and_linearMap_ML_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
